; ============================================================================
;  STAIRCASE  --  a domestic half-landing stair enclosure: 1.5 m wide, 5.2 m
;  long, open to the floor above, with a window at the half-landing and a door
;  off it.
;
;  WHY THIS SHAPE. A staircase is a narrow shaft: that is what makes a handrail
;  reachable without leaning and what the participant's own staircase at home
;  looks like. But the TOP has to be somewhere you can stand and turn around
;  comfortably -- a landing you arrive on at the very edge, with a wall in your
;  face, is unpleasant in a headset and teaches nothing. So the flight starts
;  early and the landing is nearly 2 m deep, with two standing positions on it.
;
;  LAYOUT (local coordinates; main.tscn places the room at z = +3.9)
;    z -2.6 .. -1.4   standing space at the foot, doorway in the hallway wall
;    z -1.4 ..  0.6   the flight: 8 treads, 190 mm rise / 250 mm going
;    z  0.6 .. 2.54   the half-landing, 1.545 m up: window ahead, door to one
;                     side, room to turn round in
;
;  HEAD HEIGHT AT THE TOP. Standing on the landing puts the eyes at about
;  3.2 m -- above the 2.4 m hallway wall this room borrows for its north side.
;  NorthGable fills that wall from 2.4 m to the top of the shaft, or the
;  participant looks straight over it at the underside of the roof.
;
;  WHERE YOU STAND. The teleport discs sit 0.25 m to the WEST of the middle of
;  the treads -- on the rail side, where a person actually walks up stairs --
;  so the rail is 0.35 m from the shoulder rather than 0.6 m across the tread.
;
;  RAILS. The good rail is mounted on the WEST wall over the tread edge, 0.9 m
;  above the nosing line, and extends past both ends of the flight as a real
;  one does, so it can be taken hold of before the first step and let go after
;  the last. The EAST wall has the brackets and no rail: `stairs_missing_rail`.
;
;  Architectural Fix 5.1:
;    StairGate (GatedRegion)  wraps the flight and landing. Free-aim teleport
;                             is off inside it, and no destination inside it is
;                             legal from outside it.
;    TP_Bottom                the way in, at the foot and just OUTSIDE the
;                             gate. Coming DOWN onto it still needs the rail.
;    TP_Step3 / TP_Step6      need the rail held.
;    TP_Landing               the top of the flight. No rail requirement: it is
;                             flat ground, and the rail cannot be reached from
;                             the far end of a landing. Arrives facing up the
;                             flight, so nobody lands staring down the drop.
;                             Going back DOWN needs the rail, because TP_Step6
;                             requires it -- which is the habit that matters.
;    TP_LandingBack           the far end of the landing, by the window. No
;                             rail: it is a flat floor, and being able to step
;                             back from the edge is the point of it.
;
;  Each point is selectable only from the one directly below or above, so the
;  flight is taken one step at a time, up and down. Godot yaw 0 looks along -Z
;  and this flight ascends along +Z, so ascending arrivals face 180.
; ============================================================================

[node name="Staircase" type="Node3D"]

[node name="RoomBuilder" type="Node3D" parent="."]
script = ExtResource("1_room")
window_sill_height = 2.45
window_openings = Array[Vector4]([Vector4(0, 0, 1, 1)])
trim_surface = "paint_satin"
ceiling_surface = "ceiling_plaster"
wall_surface = "plaster_wall"
floor_surface = "oak_floor"
size = Vector2(1.5, 5.2)
height = 4.0
floor_color = Color(0.45, 0.4, 0.36, 1)
wall_color = Color(0.78, 0.75, 0.7, 1)
build_ceiling = false
; Wall 1 (-Z) is the hallway's wall, doorway and all. Building it here as well
; would put two identical boxes in the same plane and make them flicker.
build_walls = Array[bool]([true, false, true, true])
openings = Array[Vector4]([])

; The hallway's wall is only 2.4 m tall and this shaft is 4 m. Without this
; filler you look straight over it from the landing.

[node name="NorthGable" type="Node3D" parent="."]
